1
00:00:09,685 --> 00:00:10,685
Yasa-chan.

2
00:00:12,405 --> 00:00:14,575
Whoa, you scared me!

3
00:00:14,705 --> 00:00:16,035
What is it?

4
00:00:16,245 --> 00:00:19,174
Call it a hunch, but...

5
00:00:19,175 --> 00:00:20,175
Yeah?

6
00:00:20,715 --> 00:00:23,345
You got a boyfriend recently, didn't you?

7
00:00:24,515 --> 00:00:27,285
Oh, stop it! No, I didn't.

8
00:00:28,555 --> 00:00:31,255
That reaction totally gives you away!

9
00:00:32,385 --> 00:00:33,395
Well, that's because...

10
00:00:34,155 --> 00:00:36,155
I didn't get a boyfriend.

11
00:00:36,465 --> 00:00:37,995
I got a girlfriend.

12
00:00:39,665 --> 00:00:41,665
A customer just asked me

13
00:00:41,795 --> 00:00:44,605
if we have any dry sake to recommend.

14
00:00:45,005 --> 00:00:48,075
Is that the new flame?

15
00:00:48,135 --> 00:00:49,316
The one in the back and the
yellow bottle should both be dry.

16
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:50,860
Not a chance in hell.

17
00:00:51,045 --> 00:00:52,575
Ah, this bottle right here.

18
00:00:53,015 --> 00:00:55,315
Got it, thanks.

19
00:01:01,355 --> 00:01:03,184
What about you, Miwa?

20
00:01:03,185 --> 00:01:05,355
Got your eye on anyone?

21
00:01:05,555 --> 00:01:06,555
Huh?

22
00:01:08,695 --> 00:01:09,695
Hey!

23
00:01:10,425 --> 00:01:12,965
They literally just broke up!

24
00:01:13,195 --> 00:01:14,395
I know, I just figured...

25
00:01:14,935 --> 00:01:18,735
I don't really have the right to, anyway.

26
00:01:58,295 --> 00:02:05,795
"How Do We Relationship?"

27
00:02:10,695 --> 00:02:13,394
(Episode 7: If There Was a Mistake)

28
00:02:13,395 --> 00:02:15,325
Can I post this on my story?

29
00:02:15,955 --> 00:02:17,065
I mean, sure,

30
00:02:17,425 --> 00:02:19,665
but people are gonna talk again.

31
00:02:19,835 --> 00:02:21,695
Asking if we got back together and stuff.

32
00:02:21,865 --> 00:02:25,105
Huh? We've been broken up for a month now.

33
00:02:25,635 --> 00:02:28,075
We're basically just
strangers at this point.

34
00:02:36,745 --> 00:02:38,185
What about that girl from before?

35
00:02:38,245 --> 00:02:39,885
Isn't she your girlfriend?

36
00:02:42,855 --> 00:02:45,725
And what would you do if I said she was?

37
00:02:47,225 --> 00:02:48,455
Well, I...

38
00:02:50,885 --> 00:02:52,295
I wouldn't do anything.

39
00:02:54,835 --> 00:02:56,665
I guess I'd feel relieved for you.

40
00:02:57,235 --> 00:02:59,705
Because I want you to meet someone great

41
00:02:59,735 --> 00:03:02,375
and be really happy.

42
00:03:05,645 --> 00:03:08,475
- Mind your own business!
- Ah!

43
00:03:09,945 --> 00:03:12,545
Besides, she's not my girlfriend anyway.

44
00:03:12,585 --> 00:03:14,684
I'm perfectly happy on my own!

45
00:03:14,685 --> 00:03:15,315
Hold on!

46
00:03:15,316 --> 00:03:17,355
How much of that are you gonna eat?!

47
00:03:21,025 --> 00:03:22,125
What about you, Miwa?

48
00:03:23,065 --> 00:03:24,924
What happened with your
senpai from high school?

49
00:03:24,925 --> 00:03:26,435
Haven't you reached out to her?

50
00:03:29,135 --> 00:03:30,535
No, I haven't.

51
00:03:32,325 --> 00:03:38,598
Besides, how could I? She's
basically the reason we broke up.

52
00:03:39,105 --> 00:03:40,315
Fair point.

53
00:03:40,945 --> 00:03:42,775
Normally, that would really piss me off.

54
00:03:46,985 --> 00:03:48,055
Right?

55
00:03:55,895 --> 00:03:56,995
Man...

56
00:03:59,425 --> 00:04:00,765
What's wrong?

57
00:04:01,835 --> 00:04:03,515
Why don't you just go get rejected by her?

58
00:04:05,005 --> 00:04:06,005
Huh?

59
00:04:06,235 --> 00:04:08,115
If you confess and get
dumped, then we're good.

60
00:04:08,275 --> 00:04:09,275
Actually,

61
00:04:09,435 --> 00:04:10,435
Hmm...

62
00:04:11,105 --> 00:04:13,415
you should just go for it
and tell her how you feel.

63
00:04:13,475 --> 00:04:15,435
You've been pining over
her for years now, right?

64
00:04:16,385 --> 00:04:17,915
I couldn't possibly...

65
00:04:18,085 --> 00:04:19,484
That just wouldn't be fair to you.

66
00:04:19,485 --> 00:04:20,514
Why not?

67
00:04:20,515 --> 00:04:22,855
If you get dumped, I won't even be mad.

68
00:04:26,155 --> 00:04:27,155
Okay, but what if...

69
00:04:28,415 --> 00:04:29,494
we actually end up dating?

70
00:04:29,495 --> 00:04:30,795
What will you do then?

71
00:04:34,435 --> 00:04:36,305
- What's so funny?
- Nothing, it's just...

72
00:04:36,365 --> 00:04:40,875
How can you say that with a straight face?

73
00:04:42,605 --> 00:04:43,605
Sorry...

74
00:04:44,805 --> 00:04:45,975
I wouldn't do anything.

75
00:04:47,375 --> 00:04:49,415
I'd just say congratulations.

76
00:05:03,645 --> 00:05:04,695
Miwa.

77
00:05:05,025 --> 00:05:08,135
You like someone, don't you?

78
00:05:08,435 --> 00:05:09,435
Huh?

79
00:05:10,635 --> 00:05:11,635
How did you know?

80
00:05:11,782 --> 00:05:16,111
Remember last time when you
said you didn't have the right?

81
00:05:16,135 --> 00:05:19,505
That basically means there's
someone on your mind.

82
00:05:22,275 --> 00:05:24,485
Ooh, silent treatment!

83
00:05:24,515 --> 00:05:27,615
You can be so sly sometimes, Miwa.

84
00:05:29,525 --> 00:05:31,125
Even though we broke up,

85
00:05:31,825 --> 00:05:33,995
I still feel guilty about it.

86
00:05:36,125 --> 00:05:38,464
I don't get that at all.

87
00:05:38,465 --> 00:05:40,835
I've never felt guilty a day in my life.

88
00:05:40,995 --> 00:05:45,935
Everyone would be way happier if
they just did whatever they wanted.

89
00:05:49,645 --> 00:05:50,645
I get it now.

90
00:05:51,745 --> 00:05:53,245
Rika, you're...

91
00:05:53,675 --> 00:05:55,375
It's not that you're a free spirit.

92
00:05:55,945 --> 00:05:58,245
You're just extremely self-centered.

93
00:06:01,295 --> 00:06:04,885
You really don't pull any punches, Miwa.

94
00:06:05,025 --> 00:06:08,025
I could never live like that.

95
00:06:09,255 --> 00:06:11,025
Really?

96
00:06:11,565 --> 00:06:17,835
Because I think you're actually
just as greedy as I am, Miwa.

97
00:06:19,225 --> 00:06:24,204
You don't want anyone to hate you,
and you always want to be in the right.

98
00:06:24,205 --> 00:06:27,925
At the end of the day, you just want to protect
this ideal image you have of yourself, right?

99
00:06:28,145 --> 00:06:30,915
It's all just to make yourself feel good.

100
00:06:33,515 --> 00:06:34,515
Well, I guess I'm just...

101
00:06:35,655 --> 00:06:37,955
greedy and selfish, then.

102
00:06:39,255 --> 00:06:41,994
Huh? What did you say?

103
00:06:41,995 --> 00:06:43,265
Wait, what? Say that again!

104
00:06:43,925 --> 00:06:44,925
Huh?

105
00:06:45,495 --> 00:06:46,565
I said,

106
00:06:47,055 --> 00:06:50,135
I'm just a greedy, selfish person!

107
00:06:55,605 --> 00:06:59,505
And that's what I love about you, Miwa.

108
00:07:04,645 --> 00:07:07,885
No, it's a girlfriend!

109
00:07:07,955 --> 00:07:11,085
Wait, a girlfriend? Seriously?!

110
00:07:11,855 --> 00:07:13,025
Not a boyfriend?

111
00:07:13,225 --> 00:07:14,525
Yep, that's right!

112
00:07:14,655 --> 00:07:16,095
Pretty wild, huh?

113
00:07:18,725 --> 00:07:20,835
I mean...

114
00:07:22,395 --> 00:07:24,235
I didn't know you were into girls too.

115
00:07:25,365 --> 00:07:26,935
Well...

116
00:07:27,005 --> 00:07:28,675
She told me,

117
00:07:28,875 --> 00:07:31,104
"It'd be such a waste

118
00:07:31,105 --> 00:07:35,745
to let only guys fall for
a girl as amazing as you."

119
00:07:35,815 --> 00:07:37,184
That's what she said!

120
00:07:37,185 --> 00:07:39,345
Smooth talker.

121
00:07:39,715 --> 00:07:43,424
And I was like, "You know
what? She has a point!"

122
00:07:43,425 --> 00:07:45,085
Wish I had your self-esteem!

123
00:07:46,655 --> 00:07:48,654
That's great, though.

124
00:07:48,655 --> 00:07:49,865
It's very you, Yuria.

125
00:07:55,435 --> 00:07:57,005
Happy for you, Yuria.

126
00:07:59,105 --> 00:08:00,605
Thank you!

127
00:08:01,135 --> 00:08:02,135
All right!

128
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:05,775
All done!

129
00:08:06,545 --> 00:08:08,445
Your hair's all set.

130
00:08:10,115 --> 00:08:11,184
Wow!

131
00:08:11,185 --> 00:08:12,685
- Thank you.
- Anytime!

132
00:08:21,115 --> 00:08:24,065
Since it's you, Yuria, I feel
like I can actually say this.

133
00:08:24,525 --> 00:08:25,525
Huh?

134
00:08:29,505 --> 00:08:30,965
To tell you the truth...

135
00:08:31,705 --> 00:08:33,535
The person I was dating before

136
00:08:34,595 --> 00:08:36,545
was actually a girl, too.

137
00:08:37,445 --> 00:08:38,445
Wait...

138
00:08:39,045 --> 00:08:40,745
Wait, seriously?!

139
00:08:41,075 --> 00:08:43,444
That makes me so happy!
We're in the same club!

140
00:08:43,445 --> 00:08:44,445
- The same club?
- Uh-huh!

141
00:08:45,895 --> 00:08:46,895
Yeah, I guess we are.

142
00:08:52,575 --> 00:08:53,575
Inuzuka.

143
00:08:56,525 --> 00:08:57,965
Shiho senpai!

144
00:09:15,915 --> 00:09:17,415
I brought you a souvenir.

145
00:09:18,085 --> 00:09:21,015
Wow, thank you!

146
00:09:24,825 --> 00:09:26,705
Is there anywhere in
particular you want to go?

147
00:09:27,025 --> 00:09:29,255
Um, well...

148
00:09:29,895 --> 00:09:31,425
I actually did...

149
00:09:31,765 --> 00:09:33,065
a little bit of...

150
00:09:33,335 --> 00:09:35,535
research on some places.

151
00:09:38,665 --> 00:09:40,635
You call this "a little bit"?!

152
00:09:41,505 --> 00:09:43,045
Let me see.

153
00:09:47,155 --> 00:09:48,985
This really takes me back.

154
00:09:49,375 --> 00:09:53,255
You used to highlight every
single thing in your textbooks, too.

155
00:09:55,055 --> 00:09:58,055
You still remember that?

156
00:09:58,125 --> 00:09:59,125
Of course.

157
00:10:00,595 --> 00:10:03,595
I remember everything about you.

158
00:10:06,395 --> 00:10:07,695
You do?

159
00:10:09,805 --> 00:10:10,905
Today,

160
00:10:11,505 --> 00:10:13,625
let's do all the things we
never got to do back then.

161
00:10:14,775 --> 00:10:15,775
Huh?

162
00:10:25,435 --> 00:10:26,685
The breeze feels amazing.

163
00:10:28,275 --> 00:10:30,085
- Is that good?
- It's delicious.

164
00:10:31,015 --> 00:10:32,385
Let me have a sip.

165
00:10:32,725 --> 00:10:33,725
Huh?

166
00:10:35,395 --> 00:10:37,565
Mmm! That is good.

167
00:10:40,055 --> 00:10:43,005
Aw, how cute! It looks great on you!

168
00:10:56,415 --> 00:10:57,545
Sae-chan.

169
00:10:58,825 --> 00:11:00,414
Look at your face right now.

170
00:11:00,415 --> 00:11:04,454
It screams, "My ex is finally
moving on to someone new."

171
00:11:04,455 --> 00:11:05,604
Does not!

172
00:11:05,605 --> 00:11:06,794
It totally does.

173
00:11:06,795 --> 00:11:07,824
Good work today!

174
00:11:07,825 --> 00:11:09,054
Hey, good work.

175
00:11:09,055 --> 00:11:11,555
Hey, Yasa-chan,

176
00:11:11,655 --> 00:11:13,965
how are things going with your girlfriend?

177
00:11:14,995 --> 00:11:16,165
Oh...

178
00:11:17,265 --> 00:11:18,605
We broke up.

179
00:11:18,865 --> 00:11:20,434
She was five-timing me.

180
00:11:20,435 --> 00:11:22,005
- Huh?
- Five...

181
00:11:22,035 --> 00:11:23,221
Five-timing?! How is that even possible?!

182
00:11:23,245 --> 00:11:25,945
I know, it was insane!

183
00:11:26,235 --> 00:11:29,545
Apparently, she tried to schedule
back-to-back dates with all of us,

184
00:11:29,795 --> 00:11:33,115
and we all ended up running
into each other at once!

185
00:11:33,655 --> 00:11:35,814
And she just stood there
grinning the whole time!

186
00:11:35,815 --> 00:11:37,685
What a total scumbag!

187
00:11:38,055 --> 00:11:39,554
Right?!

188
00:11:39,555 --> 00:11:43,385
Well, I bet that put you
off girls for good, huh?

189
00:11:43,625 --> 00:11:46,394
Huh? Why would it?

190
00:11:46,395 --> 00:11:47,065
Wait...

191
00:11:47,066 --> 00:11:50,705
Because you weren't exclusively
into girls to begin with, right?

192
00:11:51,035 --> 00:11:54,011
So having your first experience blow
up like that, wouldn't it make you think...

193
00:11:54,035 --> 00:11:56,405
"Never doing that again"?

194
00:11:57,395 --> 00:11:59,175
Hmm...

195
00:12:00,015 --> 00:12:01,275
Well,

196
00:12:01,645 --> 00:12:03,815
even if a guy did that to me,

197
00:12:04,245 --> 00:12:07,885
I wouldn't swear off men for
the rest of my life, you know?

198
00:12:09,255 --> 00:12:12,755
I don't think gender really
has anything to do with it.

199
00:12:15,895 --> 00:12:19,025
That's what I love about you, Yuria.

200
00:12:22,335 --> 00:12:23,335
Huh?

201
00:12:26,065 --> 00:12:28,575
Do you really have to get that flustered?

202
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:31,975
I'm not! Who's flustered?!

203
00:12:32,005 --> 00:12:33,345
You clearly are.

204
00:12:34,895 --> 00:12:35,995
Sorry, sorry.

205
00:12:39,195 --> 00:12:40,715
Back then, Inuzuka, you told me,

206
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:45,625
"You have to take charge of
your own happiness," remember?

207
00:12:46,895 --> 00:12:48,125
Hearing you say that

208
00:12:52,225 --> 00:12:56,865
finally made me want to
start living my life for myself.

209
00:13:00,705 --> 00:13:02,475
Even if it took me a while to get there.

210
00:13:07,615 --> 00:13:08,615
So really,

211
00:13:11,145 --> 00:13:14,055
you're my savior, Inuzuka.

212
00:13:15,025 --> 00:13:17,785
You're someone very special to me.

213
00:13:20,555 --> 00:13:22,555
I just wanted to tell you that today.

214
00:13:25,325 --> 00:13:26,335
Thank you,

215
00:13:27,335 --> 00:13:28,335
Inuzuka.

216
00:13:32,265 --> 00:13:35,035
Your savior, huh?

217
00:13:47,415 --> 00:13:48,755
Shiho senpai.

218
00:13:50,235 --> 00:13:51,235
I...

219
00:13:54,425 --> 00:13:56,025
I don't want to just be your savior.

220
00:13:58,425 --> 00:13:59,735
Not your savior,

221
00:14:00,515 --> 00:14:01,995
and not just your underclassman.

222
00:14:04,935 --> 00:14:06,535
I want to be your girlfriend.

223
00:14:09,215 --> 00:14:10,304
I'm in love with you,

224
00:14:10,305 --> 00:14:11,575
Shiho senpai.

225
00:14:13,815 --> 00:14:15,475
Ever since high school,

226
00:14:16,645 --> 00:14:18,085
I've always been in love with you.

227
00:14:21,855 --> 00:14:23,085
Inuzuka...

228
00:14:35,665 --> 00:14:36,735
I'm sorry.

229
00:14:40,435 --> 00:14:42,575
I can't go out with you.

230
00:14:45,015 --> 00:14:46,674
It's not that I don't like you,

231
00:14:46,675 --> 00:14:48,645
and it's not because you're a girl.

232
00:14:54,495 --> 00:14:56,585
I dated someone a while back.

233
00:14:57,715 --> 00:14:59,795
He was a guy.

234
00:15:00,595 --> 00:15:02,555
He confessed to me, too,

235
00:15:04,095 --> 00:15:06,535
and I respected him as
a person, so I said yes.

236
00:15:08,995 --> 00:15:11,405
I figured we could make it work somehow.

237
00:15:15,695 --> 00:15:16,695
Yeah...

238
00:15:18,235 --> 00:15:19,235
But in the end,

239
00:15:20,955 --> 00:15:21,955
I just couldn't do it.

240
00:15:24,785 --> 00:15:27,015
My heart wasn't fully in it,

241
00:15:28,215 --> 00:15:30,085
and I think he picked up on that.

242
00:15:34,025 --> 00:15:35,625
I ended up hurting him really badly.

243
00:15:38,865 --> 00:15:40,895
It was so irresponsible of me.

244
00:15:45,395 --> 00:15:46,395
And I...

245
00:15:47,135 --> 00:15:49,405
I don't want to make
the same mistake again.

246
00:15:49,975 --> 00:15:53,775
Especially not with someone who
means as much to me as you do.

247
00:15:57,735 --> 00:15:58,915
I wouldn't care...

248
00:16:00,255 --> 00:16:03,401
Even if we were only together for a fleeting
moment, that would be enough for me.

249
00:16:03,425 --> 00:16:05,455
Could we not even have that?

250
00:16:09,495 --> 00:16:10,495
I'm sorry.

251
00:16:12,795 --> 00:16:13,795
Well then, let me...

252
00:16:15,365 --> 00:16:16,865
put it another way.

253
00:16:18,365 --> 00:16:20,705
I really didn't want to have to say this,

254
00:16:24,375 --> 00:16:26,855
but the courage it takes to
face the world and its judgment...

255
00:16:28,195 --> 00:16:29,545
I just don't have it in me.

256
00:16:33,355 --> 00:16:34,355
But...

257
00:16:37,155 --> 00:16:39,185
there are people out there who understand!

258
00:16:39,655 --> 00:16:40,855
I know that.

259
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:42,625
But still...

260
00:16:43,465 --> 00:16:45,565
Just knowing there are
people who won't understand

261
00:16:47,195 --> 00:16:48,195
terrifies me.

262
00:16:51,335 --> 00:16:52,975
And it's not just the hostility.

263
00:16:55,375 --> 00:16:57,105
It's the overbearing concern,

264
00:16:58,315 --> 00:16:59,315
and the pity...

265
00:17:01,195 --> 00:17:03,845
I've had enough of all of it.

266
00:17:09,625 --> 00:17:11,485
I really do care about you, Inuzuka.

267
00:17:15,335 --> 00:17:16,335
But...

268
00:17:17,725 --> 00:17:18,725
I'm sorry.

269
00:17:25,035 --> 00:17:26,264
I'm truly sorry.

270
00:17:26,265 --> 00:17:27,465
Okay, I got it!

271
00:17:28,715 --> 00:17:30,245
I understand completely.

272
00:17:33,415 --> 00:17:36,215
I'm really glad I got to
hear how you honestly feel.

273
00:17:40,175 --> 00:17:41,885
Thanks to you, I finally have closure.

274
00:17:42,755 --> 00:17:44,155
Thank you, senpai.

275
00:17:57,135 --> 00:17:59,705
Things must feel pretty
awkward for you right now, huh?

276
00:18:00,875 --> 00:18:05,305
Honestly, it's pretty awkward for me too...

277
00:18:05,375 --> 00:18:06,915
And a little embarrassing.

278
00:18:07,755 --> 00:18:09,635
So let's just call it a
day and part ways here.

279
00:18:10,615 --> 00:18:11,615
Are you sure?

280
00:18:14,415 --> 00:18:15,415
Well,

281
00:18:16,525 --> 00:18:18,325
I'll reach out to you again later.

282
00:18:19,895 --> 00:18:21,295
Get home safe.

283
00:18:22,725 --> 00:18:24,065
I'll get going now!

284
00:19:16,685 --> 00:19:17,715
Miwa?

285
00:19:17,915 --> 00:19:19,045
Are you okay?

286
00:19:19,555 --> 00:19:20,855
I came to check on you.

287
00:19:22,285 --> 00:19:23,285
You didn't have to.

288
00:19:24,125 --> 00:19:26,795
I'm fine. Just leave me alone.

289
00:19:26,805 --> 00:19:28,155
How is this "fine"?!

290
00:19:28,255 --> 00:19:30,125
You've skipped classes for a whole week!

291
00:19:30,365 --> 00:19:31,795
Are you feeling sick or something?

292
00:19:32,445 --> 00:19:34,365
I'm fine, just go home already.

293
00:19:34,395 --> 00:19:35,795
Wait, what?

294
00:19:42,445 --> 00:19:44,705
Keep it down, you're
gonna bother the neighbors!

295
00:19:50,915 --> 00:19:52,515
Your room is a total pigsty!

296
00:19:53,585 --> 00:19:55,055
And it's pitch dark in here.

297
00:19:58,045 --> 00:19:59,455
I'm opening the window!

298
00:20:13,005 --> 00:20:15,035
Would you just get out of here already?

299
00:20:16,845 --> 00:20:18,405
What's with the attitude?!

300
00:20:19,445 --> 00:20:20,974
Anyway, have you seen a doctor?

301
00:20:20,975 --> 00:20:22,175
Did you take your temperature?

302
00:20:22,445 --> 00:20:23,915
I don't know.

303
00:20:24,815 --> 00:20:26,045
Who cares.

304
00:20:26,515 --> 00:20:27,515
Huh?

305
00:20:41,435 --> 00:20:43,465
Oh, right!

306
00:20:45,465 --> 00:20:49,705
I bought a bunch of groceries!
I'll whip up a Saeko Special for you!

307
00:20:51,045 --> 00:20:53,175
I didn't ask for your help.

308
00:20:53,215 --> 00:20:54,515
What was that?

309
00:20:54,605 --> 00:20:56,285
Can't hear you!

310
00:21:06,955 --> 00:21:08,295
Serves me right...

311
00:21:14,505 --> 00:21:16,405
Here, just take one bite.

312
00:21:16,465 --> 00:21:17,535
Come on.

313
00:21:41,195 --> 00:21:42,855
Eat up and go back to sleep.

314
00:21:44,225 --> 00:21:46,025
I'll come by again tomorrow.

315
00:21:47,495 --> 00:21:48,995
Don't bother.

316
00:21:51,105 --> 00:21:53,075
Knew you'd say that.

317
00:21:54,075 --> 00:21:56,035
Look at you, you're a total mess right now.

318
00:21:57,145 --> 00:21:59,645
If I hadn't shown up, you
probably would've starved to death!

319
00:22:02,645 --> 00:22:04,045
I don't care if I starve.

320
00:22:05,015 --> 00:22:06,245
I might as well just die.

321
00:22:07,355 --> 00:22:08,385
I wanna die.

322
00:22:08,815 --> 00:22:11,525
Oh, so that's how we're talking now?!

323
00:22:11,955 --> 00:22:13,655
Then I'm confiscating these noodles!

324
00:22:15,495 --> 00:22:17,625
People who wanna die
don't need food anyway!

325
00:22:20,585 --> 00:22:21,585
Mmm, so good!

326
00:22:21,765 --> 00:22:23,335
Am I an udon genius or what?

327
00:22:24,965 --> 00:22:29,005
As long as you stay alive, I'll make
this for you whenever you want!

328
00:22:31,645 --> 00:22:32,645
Stop it.

329
00:22:35,565 --> 00:22:37,415
You're only making me feel more pathetic.

330
00:22:37,845 --> 00:22:39,405
Honestly, you're being really annoying.

331
00:22:40,655 --> 00:22:43,185
Huh? What do you mean, "annoying"?!

332
00:22:43,785 --> 00:22:45,585
You're the annoying one here!

333
00:22:46,245 --> 00:22:47,885
What the hell are you moping around for?!

334
00:22:48,425 --> 00:22:50,185
Stop acting so fragile
just to get sympathy!

335
00:22:50,895 --> 00:22:53,464
Shut up and go home already!

336
00:22:53,465 --> 00:22:54,495
Huh?

337
00:22:55,325 --> 00:22:57,505
Do you really hate me that much?!

338
00:23:14,555 --> 00:23:15,555
What are you doing?

339
00:23:16,755 --> 00:23:18,255
Let go of me.

340
00:23:26,895 --> 00:23:30,335
Please don't leave me...

341
00:23:31,865 --> 00:23:33,505
Don't leave me all alone...

342
00:23:38,995 --> 00:23:41,495
(Final Episode Preview)

343
00:23:42,825 --> 00:23:43,984
Let's do it one more time.

344
00:23:43,985 --> 00:23:45,414
We make pretty good
friends with benefits, right?

345
00:23:45,415 --> 00:23:46,785
We're the worst.

346
00:23:46,815 --> 00:23:48,654
Even though you can't
even bear to look at me.

347
00:23:48,655 --> 00:23:50,225
I've wanted to die this whole time.

348
00:23:50,255 --> 00:23:53,525
There's no way we can go
back to being friends now.
